  "optoEnabledText": "Skip to main content\nSkip to navigation\nNavigated to Animal\nWorkspace\n▸\nre\nremy\n▾\nValidation & Export\n⌨\nKeyboard shortcuts\nremy\nanimal ID\nRattus norvegicus · M\n⟳\nSaving…\n⋮\nWild Type\nM\nRattus norvegicus\nb. 2023-01-10\n8 probes — CA1, CA3, PFC\nConfig v1\nTeam: Guidera, Jennifer, Comrie, Alison\nOptogenetics\nDAY WORK\nRecording Days\n1\n›\nValidation & Export\n0 ready\n›\nANIMAL SETUP\nElectrode Groups\n8\n›\nRecording System\n1\n›\nCameras\n2\n›\nTask Types\n›\nOptogenetics\n●\nincomplete\n›\n⚠\nAffects all 1 day\n\nOpto configured · 2 of 4\n\nOptogenetics Setup\n\nThis is the animal's implanted opto setup (excitation source, optical fiber, virus injection, stimulation software) — set it once here. What was actually stimulated is recorded per recording day in that day's Epochs step, scoped to the epochs it ran; a day or epoch with no stimulation needs nothing here.\n\nThis animal has optogenetics\n\nThis app blocks export until every optogenetics section below is complete; still missing: a complete excitation source, a complete optical fiber, a complete virus injection. Separately, if a partial file like this were fed straight to the conversion tool, it would silently drop the entire optogenetics block with no error — which is exactly what this export gate prevents.\n\nExcitation source\nSetup name\nHardware model name\nDescription\nWavelength (nm)\nSource power (W)\nIntensity (W/m²)\nOptical fibers\nAdd optical fiber\nVirus injections\nAdd virus injection\nStimulation software\nOptogenetic stimulation software\nCopyright © 2026 Loren Frank Lab\nThe University of California at San Francisco\n",
