    "text": "Skip to main content\nSkip to navigation\nNavigated to Home - Animal Selection\nWorkspace\nValidation & Export\n⌨\nKeyboard shortcuts\nAnimals › New animal\nNew animal — guided setup\n\nEnter once what stays the same for this animal across every recording day. Recording days reuse all of this; you'll only revisit it on a re-implant.\n\nStarting fresh below, or Import a YAML… · Copy from another animal…\n\n1\nIdentity\n2\nElectrodes\n3\nCameras\n4\nOptogenetics\noptional\n5\nTasks\n6\nRecording system\nPre-filled — review\n7\nTeam\nIdentity\n\nWho this animal is. Fixed for the animal's life — set carefully; it can't drift day to day.\n\nSubject ID\nMust be unique. Case folds to one key (RS10 = rs10). No slashes (DANDI). Locked once the animal is created.\nUse only letters, numbers, and hyphens (no underscores — the converter splits filenames on them)\nSpecies\nRat (Rattus norvegicus)\nMouse (Mus musculus)\nMarmoset (Callithrix jacchus)\nRhesus macaque (Macaca mulatta)\nOther (specify)…\nLatin binomial — DANDI rejects free text like “Rat”.\nSex\nMale (M)\nFemale (F)\nUnknown (U)\nSingle letter (NWB/DANDI), not “Male”.\nGenotype\nGenetic background — not the strain. Use “Wild-type” for unmodified.\nWeight (grams)\nDate of Birth\nDescription\nFree-text note. Leave blank to auto-generate one from genotype and species.\n← Back\nSave draft\nNext →\nCopyright © 2026 Loren Frank Lab\nThe University of California at San Francisco\n",
    "readOnly": true
  }
